  "definition": "Benzene is a clear, colorless, highly flammable liquid chemical found in crude oil and used in industry as a solvent and to make other chemicals. Exposure can cause neurological symptoms, damage bone marrow and the immune system, and increase the risk of certain blood and lymphatic cancers.",
